// Question 13 (10 Marks): Analogy-based question: Treat MongoDB as a library
// system: Server -> Database -> Collection -> Document -> Field is like
// Library -> Section -> Shelf -> Book -> Information inside the book. Using
// this analogy, explain the hierarchy and then write commands to select
// collegeDB, inspect its collections, and display all documents in students.
// A server is the library, a database is a section, a collection is a shelf,
// a document is one book, and each field is a piece of information in a book.
use collegeDB

// List the database's collections (shelves).
show collections

// Display every student document (book) and its fields (information).
db.students.find();
